# HACK! Restart the PipeWire stack when an ALSA sound card appears or
# disappears.
#
# This script is not installed by the package and its code is commented out:
# it outlines one way to handle such events. To use it, install it as
# /etc/hotplug.d/sound/20-pipewire and remove the comment markers in front of
# the code.
#
# OpenWrt uses libudev-zero (no udevd rules/properties), so the udev-based ALSA
# monitor of the session manager only sees the sound cards present when it
# starts: libudev-zero's monitor listens on netlink group 0x4, to which udevd
# would rebroadcast the kernel uevents, and nothing does so here. A card
# hot-plugged at runtime therefore needs a stack restart to appear. This hook
# automates that, at the cost of a few seconds of audio interruption per
# plug/unplug event.
#
# SERVICES lists further services that are PipeWire clients and are restarted
# along with the stack.
#
# NOTE: sourced (not executed) by hotplug-call - no exit/shebang, no set -e.

